### Describe the feature you'd like to request

Generic types cannot be passed to client methods, they are taken from the router definitions, which means they are always set to the default value.
This deprives the functions of flexibility and functionality.
Example:
```ts
import { createTRPCProxyClient } from "@trpc/client";
import { initTRPC } from "@trpc/server";

type InputType = { optional: boolean; };
type Res<T> = ({ field: number; }) & (T extends { optional: true; } ? { optional_field: number; } : {});

function fn<Input extends InputType>(input: Input) {
    return {
        field: 123,
        ...(input.optional ? { optional_field: 456 } : {})
    } as Res<Input>;
}

const t = initTRPC.create({/* ... */ });
const router = t.router({
    qwe: t.procedure
        .input((value) => (value as InputType))
        .query(({ input }) => fn(input))
});
type Router = typeof router;
const client = createTRPCProxyClient<Router>({/* ... */ } as any); // browser client
const caller = router.createCaller({}); // server client
```
```ts
const { optional_field: test1 } = fn({ optional: true }); // no error, right
const { optional_field: test2 } = fn({ optional: false }); // error, no field, right
const { optional_field: test3 } = client.qwe.query({ optional: true }); // error, no field, wrong
const { optional_field: test4 } = client.qwe.query({ optional: false }); // error, no field, right
const { optional_field: test5 } = caller.qwe({ optional: true }); // error, no field, wrong
const { optional_field: test6 } = caller.qwe({ optional: false }); // error, no field, right
```

### Describe the solution you'd like to see

I don't know if it will be possible to do this.

